    "narrative": "The starting lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP is headlined by **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.13) and **Mickey Moniak** (69.49), both of whom capitalize on favorable matchups against right-handed pitching to secure elite efficiency ratings. **Tyler Soderstrom** draws a significant park boost and a soft matchup against Kumar Rocker, while **Mickey Moniak** benefits from a strong dynamic platoon edge (+14%) and favorable wind conditions that outweigh his park penalty. **Seiya Suzuki** also remains a core start (66.61), buoyed by a prime #2 hole placement and a matchup against a mediocre Liberatore. Meanwhile, **Austin Riley** (62.71) serves as a high-floor play despite a lower batting order, as he benefits from the slow delivery of Pfaadt, which creates a prime opportunity to chase our scarcity-driven stolen base targets.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Travis Bazzana** (51.20) and **Cole Young** (50.03), both of whom were relegated to the bench despite respectable scores. **Travis Bazzana** was the closest to cracking the starting nine, but he ultimately lacked the volatility and elite efficiency profile required to displace the high-scoring platoon bats like **Mickey Moniak** or the speed-chasing utility of **Brice Turang**. We are exercising caution with **Corbin Carroll** (52.80) and **Gabriel Moreno** (43.65) today; both face Chris Sale, whose 2.88 xERA makes him a dangerous hurdle that significantly drags down their raw projections. With **James Wood** still sidelined on the IL, we are closely monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Brice Turang**, **Jose Caballero**, **Max Muncy**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Henry Bolte**, **Mickey Moniak**, and **Isaac Paredes**, as any late-breaking shifts in the batting order could necessitate immediate adjustments to our efficiency modeling.",
